    <statement><p>A street light is at the top of a 26 ft pole.  A 5 ft tall girl
walks along a straight path away from the pole with a speed of 7 ft/sec.</p>
<p>At what rate is the tip of her shadow moving away from the light (ie. away
from the <alert> top </alert> of the pole) when the girl is 31 ft away from the pole?</p>
<p>Answer: <fillin characters="40" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
<p>How fast is her shadow lengthening?</p>
<p>Answer: <fillin characters="40" name="AnSwEr0002"/></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>\frac{\left(31+7.38095\right)\mathopen{}\left(7+1.66667\right)}{46.3584}</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>\frac{7}{\frac{26}{5}-1}</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
  </static>
